<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.AFRICAN DEC M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWS 13.73 PCT.</title>
<headline>S.AFRICAN DEC M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWS 13.73 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's year-on-year broadly defined M3 money supply grew 13.73 percent in December, preliminary Reserve Bank figures show.</p>
<p>November M3 growth was revised to 15.18 percent from a preliminary 15.32 percent.</p>
<p>Annual private sector credit growth was 15.75 percent, preliminary figures showed, against a revised 17.13 percent in November.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economist forecast M3 year-on-year growth of 14.3 percent from 15.32 in November while private credit was seen expanding 16.3 percent against 17.10 percent.  </p>
<p>Detailed data (Percentage changes over 12 months):</p>
